{ instr_size.init - the bytes an instruction of each opcode takes when
  made with its default operands (44 and 12 for each operand), by
  opcode (opc$t's whole range, 0..383; opc$adj_move (211) is the last
  with a size): a DSEE derived object of be_com/opcodes.def (the opcode
  generator's), included by iv and lir after the opcode enumeration.

  The file holds the declaration only: each includer opens the var
  section it goes in (iv a plain `var': its data +0; lir `var
  (lir_readonly_tables)': that section's first table, 0x2BDA2C, read by
  lir_$opt_new_instruction for an instruction of default size).

  No Apollo copy survives; reconstructed from cc.a88k: iv's .rwdi
  records (A5 0x486500, 212 words) and lir's copy, the section
  lir_readonly_tables (+0 .. +0x2FF: the same 212 words, then zeros to
  word 383; the next table, solution_kind.init's, starts at +0x300), so
  the table has 384 entries (docs/questions.md 205, 221; translator
  PA6).  The variable's name is not known from the original. }

  instr_size: array [0..383] of integer := [
    0, 56, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68,  { 0 }
    68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 68, 92, 92, 92, 92,  { 16 }
    92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92,  { 32 }
    116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116,  { 48 }
    116, 116, 116, 116, 68, 56, 56, 68, 68, 68, 80, 80, 68, 80, 80, 92,  { 64 }
    104, 92, 104, 92, 92, 92, 92, 80, 80, 80, 92, 92, 92, 92, 92, 104,  { 80 }
    104, 92, 92, 92, 68, 68, 68, 116, 116, 116, 104, 104, 104, 116, 92, 68,  { 96 }
    56, 68, 56, 104, 80, 44, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 116, 128, 104, 68, 68,  { 112 }
    68, 164, 152, 152, 80, 80, 68, 68, 68, 80, 80, 80, 80, 80, 80, 92,  { 128 }
    80, 68, 80, 80, 80, 92, 68, 80, 68, 80, 92, 92, 80, 68, 68, 92,  { 144 }
    92, 104, 92, 104, 104, 104, 92, 80, 104, 80, 104, 128, 128, 104, 80, 80,  { 160 }
    128, 128, 80, 80, 80, 92, 92, 104, 128, 128, 80, 80, 68, 116, 116, 80,  { 176 }
    44, 44, 68, 68, 80, 80, 56, 56, 56, 44, 44, 80, 56, 56, 56, 56,  { 192 }
    44, 44, 44, 56,  { 208 }
    172 of 0];  { 212 .. 383: no .rwdi record (iv), zero words (lir) }
